{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "mos-native-width-pressure-sets",
  "title": "Opt-in native-width register classes change default-mode register pressure sets and code",
  "status": "confirmed",
  "summary": "Split #321-1 (a359c6b1d73c) adds the single-member classes Ac16, Xc16 and Yc16 for the opt-in 65816 native widths. TableGen derives pressure sets from them: the MOS pressure tables grow from 6 sets to 14 and lose MOSAsmParamRegClass. MachineLICM, MachineSink and the scheduler read those tables in every mode, so default-mode code changes. Against upstream 06bc967d2668 on the split's fixed 90-input set, 18 of 90 mos6502 and 33 of 90 plain mosw65816 results differ, adding +3,478 bytes on mos6502 and +3,202 bytes on mosw65816. Candidate (Phase A, not yet applied to the series or downstream): let GeneratePressureSet = 0 on Ac16/Xc16/Yc16 restores upstream's PressureNameTable/PressureLimitTable exactly and makes default output byte-identical to upstream on all 90 inputs in both modes, in asm and object. At #321-1, +mos-a16 and +mos-a16,+mos-xy16 output also becomes identical to upstream plain mosw65816 (-3,202 bytes). At series head c33eb63d65a3 the change removes 3,515 bytes (mos6502) and 3,379 bytes (mosw65816) of default-mode code, but native output grows by 539 bytes (+mos-a16: 21 inputs larger, 13 smaller) and by 217 bytes (+mos-a16,+mos-xy16: 21 larger, 10 smaller). That growth is unexplained and escalated.",
  "report": "docs/plans/2026-09-30-native-register-pressure-sets.md",
  "reproducer_origin": "original",
  "attribution": [
    "Record, baseline, candidate experiment and evidence: Claude Code 2.1.285 (claude --version at run time; t3-opus-med subagent), model Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5), medium reasoning effort (agent definition); session https://claude.ai/code/session_01HAKZG571yi9zqmAeWQZVtk. Original observation (split 321-01 pressure-set diff and default-mode size growth) and plan: the #320/#321 split work and the planning session (Claude Code 2.1.283, model claude-opus-5-5, xhigh reasoning effort, session f79adc39-72b4-4dc5-abc1-849c14c5ce96, as recorded in the plan)."
  ],
